From 3f35efd71787a00293d5f14e65c94abbdb760942 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 16:15:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] borg: reset the home-grab skip flag for each home ware

borg_think_home_grab_useless() skips a home ware that the Borg's sale
history says it has just stored at home, so that it does not take it
straight back out.  The skip_it flag it uses is cleared once, when it
is declared, and never again inside the ware loop.  Once one ware
matches the history, every later ware in the home is skipped as well,
whether or not it matches.

With a recently stored Potion of Cure Critical Wounds in the first home
slot and a Scroll of Light, which adds nothing to the home, after it,
the Borg therefore leaves the scroll at home instead of taking it out to
sell.

Clear the flag at the start of each ware's history check, as the
home-buy step (borg_think_home_buy_useful) already does.

Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#29.
---
 src/borg/borg-store-buy.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-store-buy.c b/src/borg/borg-store-buy.c
index e6841a92f..a1c3e674b 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-store-buy.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-store-buy.c
@@ -883,6 +883,7 @@ bool borg_think_home_grab_useless(void)
             continue;
 
         /* skip stuff if we sold bought it */
+        skip_it = false;
         for (p = 0; p < sold_item_num; p++) {
             if (sold_item_tval[p] == item->tval
                 && sold_item_sval[p] == item->sval
